   ✦ The run begins in 1937: everybody is 6 years older than in January 1931.
   ✦ The papers of the years before: 22 days remembered.
   ◆ Ada's past: "He had been very regular in his payments, and always gave her a sovereign on a Saturday night."
   ◆ Arthur's past: "He never spent more than he could afford."
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He always treated his clerks liberally, and never deducted fines.
   📅 Ada means to: Tuesday: washes up the tea-cups and sets the place straight | Wednesday: cleans boots | Thursday: looks for work | Friday: pays the rent, and on Saturday she would go marketing
   📅 Arthur means to: Tuesday: posts his monthly statement to the chief at Moorgate
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Tuesday: audits the cash-book | Wednesday: posts the ledger | Thursday: balances the cash
   ✦ Mr. Thomas retires; Mr. Hale is chief clerk.
   ♥ Bert is walking out with Rose Gurney, who works at the jam factory.
